From def84d9cb574e1bdbed83eeea638ff82dce32610 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 23:05:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 104/638] [AROS] Use pipes for libevent wakeups

AI_PHASE: Chromium hosted runtime bring-up

AI_STATUS: implemented

ROOT_CAUSE: The AROS evutil_socketpair branch returned ENOSYS even though signal.c already treats the wakeup pair as read/write file descriptors. Every worker MessagePumpLibevent therefore failed in evsignal_init before entering its loop.

FIX_REASON: A POSIX pipe supplies exactly the unidirectional wakeup behavior used by the AROS signal handler and avoids involving task-owned bsdsocket.library state.

SCOPE: third_party/libevent/evutil.c

VALIDATION: ninja obj/third_party/libevent/libevent/evutil.o

RISK: Low. The change is AROS-only and preserves the existing libevent fd pair contract.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-aros-port-roadmap

Continues: 8df7662723 [AROS] Use Exec tasks for thread identity
---
 third_party/libevent/evutil.c | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/third_party/libevent/evutil.c b/third_party/libevent/evutil.c
index 191175fa06..8d73ee26d7 100644
--- a/third_party/libevent/evutil.c
+++ b/third_party/libevent/evutil.c
@@ -68,9 +68,7 @@ evutil_socketpair(int family, int type, int protocol, int fd[2])
 	(void)family;
 	(void)type;
 	(void)protocol;
-	(void)fd;
-	errno = ENOSYS;
-	return -1;
+	return pipe(fd);
 #elif !defined(WIN32)
 	return socketpair(family, type, protocol, fd);
 #else
